      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 19th‑century railroad, the Knoxville, Cumberland Gap and Louisville Railroad, ran through Corryton, turning it from an agricultural hamlet into a suburban town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corryton%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Corryton Historical Society, founded in 1987, houses a museum in a historic one‑room schoolhouse built in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/29067",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The society hosts an annual Heritage Day celebration featuring music, food, and traditional crafts that brings residents together.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
